# Copy to .env. Every variable is declared and validated at boot in env.ts.

# Keys and sign-ins are easiest in Settings → Providers (docs/providers.md).
# Env vars work too: the provider's usual one, read by pi-ai. A Claude
# subscription token (`claude setup-token`) goes in ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_TOKEN.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model new sessions start with until a default is picked in Settings.
# PI_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5

# Small, cheap model for quick side jobs: session titles and commit message
# drafts. Unset: titles are the prompt's first words, messages are by hand.
# PI_FAST_MODEL=openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5

# The agent's web_search and web_fetch tools (Exa; free plan is fine). Or
# add the key in Settings → Providers.
# Get one at https://dashboard.exa.ai/api-keys
# EXA_API_KEY=
